/-!
# The proper-core kernel argument

The reductions below concern the actual commutator kernel `[⟨Jᴹ⟩,D ∩ L]`.
They establish its coprime decomposition and show how the source involution
profile, torus transitivity and nonsquareness give the normal kernel needed
by the proper-core complement construction.

The construction of the abelian base and the torus/nonsquare source inputs
remain to be proved. Final assembly of those inputs belongs in this module.
Source: GLS, Volume 4, Chapter 2, Lemmas 15.6–15.7,
`refs/KGroup/GLS4/Chapter2.tex`, lines 2703–2750.
-/
